patrone-remote-desktop (0.5.9) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Changing the mouse pointer no longer ends the session on the screen and
    goes back to the login screen. The screen's client watched the desktop's
    cursor theme, and when it changes, SDL frees the theme's images but keeps
    them as its default cursor, which it shows at every change of pointer, so
    the next one attached an image that was gone and cage dropped the client.
    The client draws the pointers the desktop sends, so it no longer gets a
    session bus and doesn't watch the theme.

