patrone-remote-desktop (0.5.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Sound in Hyper-V's enhanced session. GNOME Remote Desktop sends its
    first sound message, the formats it can play, right after asking
    VMConnect to open the sound channel (AUDIO_PLAYBACK_DVC), without
    waiting for the answer, and FreeRDP's proxy drops anything on a dynamic
    channel that isn't open yet. VMConnect never heard the formats, and the
    desktop gave up on sound ten seconds later, every session. The plugin
    now answers the desktop itself that the channel can't be opened, and
    the desktop sends sound over the older static channel (rdpsnd), which
    the proxy passes on as it comes. The microphone's channel waits for its
    answer, so it isn't affected.

