patrone-remote-desktop (0.5.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Hyper-V's enhanced session (VMConnect): a login screen in VMConnect's
    window, then the account's own desktop, with the clipboard, sound and a
    screen that follows the window (the user, 2026-10-28). A second proxy
    listens on vsock port 3389, which only the Hyper-V host can reach
    (patrone-remote-desktop-vmconnect.service, on Hyper-V only). Its plugin
    (patrone-vmconnect) shows each connection Patrone's login screen first
    (libexec/greeter, one per connection), which has the password checked
    with PAM (auth --vmconnect: any account that may sign in at the
    computer) and then hands the proxy to the account's GNOME Remote
    Desktop, while VMConnect stays connected. Network Remote Desktop is
    unchanged, and whether it's on doesn't matter to this.
  * Tells VMConnect when the account has signed in, as Windows does: until
    then VMConnect keeps its window one size, though the desktop offers it
    display control. The plugin logs display control and the sizes
    VMConnect asks for, and the service logs to syslog, so its lines reach
    the journal as they happen.
  * Builds against cairo, Pango and xkbcommon for the login screen.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:40:00 -0500

