patrone-remote-desktop (0.4.5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Settings can turn Remote Desktop on: Patrone's build of GNOME Settings
    has an "Enable Remote Desktop" switch in System > Remote Desktop >
    Remote Login. It runs a helper (libexec/settings) through pkexec, for
    the account using Settings: turning it on (an administrator's
    password) runs "patrone-remote-desktop enable" and adds the account to
    the remote-desktop group, turning it off runs "disable", and its state
    comes from the helper's status. A polkit policy
    (org.patrone.remote-desktop.policy) allows the same in Patrone's
    desktops, which have no seat, as at a seat.
  * Settings records what NLA checks right away: it asks for the account's
    own password once, and "auth --confirm" checks it with Remote
    Desktop's PAM service and writes its NT hash, so a new member can
    connect without first signing in again with its password.
  * Depends on pkexec.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:00:00 -0500

