patrone-remote-desktop (0.4.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Signing in on the screen joins the account's desktop instead of ending
    it: GNOME's login screen called the desktop (which runs with no seat) a
    conflicting session and ended it. A login-screen extension
    (patrone-login@patroneos.com, enabled through GDM's settings) leaves
    seatless sessions out of that check.
  * Patrone Desktop is the screen's only session: Ubuntu's ubuntu.desktop is
    moved aside (a plain GNOME session on the screen would end the account's
    desktop), and a hidden patrone-gnome.desktop is the session background
    desktops run. Accounts that remembered Ubuntu's session get Patrone
    Desktop, GDM's first remaining choice.

